            "author": {
              "@type": "Person",
              "name": "lutzflcat"
            },
            "reviewBody": "It was VERY easy to make, and it ended up tasting exactly like I thought it would...orange cornbread. Typically, johnny cake is cooked as a pancake, but I was OK with baking and cutting it into squares. I cut back on the milk a little and added some orange juice, but even with the orange zest, I would have liked more orange flavor. This was OK, served it with butter and maple syrup for breakfast, but not sure I like it well enough to make again.",
